,"Hunter X Hunter",[26],"TV","Manga",148,"Finished Airing",false,{"from":47,"to":48,"prop":49,"string":58},"2011-10-02T00:00:00+00:00","2014-09-24T00:00:00+00:00",{"from":50,"to":54},{"day":51,"month":52,"year":53},2,10,2011,{"day":55,"month":56,"year":57},24,9,2014,"Oct 2, 2011 to Sep 24, 2014","23 min per ep","PG-13 - Teens 13 or older",9.03,1989683,8,3204718,230221,"Hunters devote themselves to accomplishing hazardous tasks, all from traversing the world's uncharted territories to locating rare items and monsters. Before becoming a Hunter, one must pass the Hunter Examination—a high-risk selection process in which most applicants end up handicapped or worse, deceased.\n\nAmbitious participants who challenge the notorious exam carry their own reason. What drives 12-year-old Gon Freecss is finding Ging, his father and a Hunter himself. Believing that he will meet his father by becoming a Hunter, Gon takes the first step to walk the same path.\n\nDuring the Hunter Examination, Gon befriends the medical student Leorio Paladiknight, the vindictive Kurapika, and ex-assassin Killua Zoldyck. While their motives vastly differ from each other, they band together for a common goal and begin to venture into a perilous world.\n\n[Written by MAL Rewrite]","","fall",{"day":70,"time":71,"timezone":72,"string":73},"Sundays","10:55","Asia\u002FTokyo","Sundays at 10:55 (JST)",[75,80,84],{"mal_id":76,"type":77,"name":78,"url":79},29,"anime","VAP","https:\u002F\u002Fmyanimelist.net\u002Fanime\u002Fproducer\u002F29\u002FVAP",{"mal_id":81,"type":77,"name":82,"url":83},1003,"Nippon Television Network","https:\u002F\u002Fmyanimelist.net\u002Fanime\u002Fproducer\u002F1003\u002FNippon_Television_Network",{"mal_id":85,"type":77,"name":86,"url":87},1365,"Shueisha","https:\u002F\u002Fmyanimelist.net\u002Fanime\u002Fproducer\u002F1365\u002FShueisha",[89],{"mal_id":90,"type":77,"name":91,"url":92},119,"VIZ Media","https:\u002F\u002Fmyanimelist.net\u002Fanime\u002Fproducer\u002F119\u002FVIZ_Medi